A field summary names a table whose header never closes on its line (`[[bin`, in a half-edited
file) by that line alone, even when the parser recovers it with the brackets of a later header,
so the file summary stays on one line; its fields are the keys the parser put in that table.
== args
input
== file input/Cargo.toml
[[bin

name = "x"
[[bin]]
name = "y"
== stdout
glob view: input
input/Cargo.toml (5 lines): [[bin {name = "y"}
== stderr
== exit 0
